WEBVTT

1
00:00:11.757 --> 00:00:15.820
the next morning, the doctor climbed up from Dorfli with Peter and the goats.

2
00:00:16.941 --> 00:00:20.825
When they reached the hut, Heidi was waiting for them with Daisy and Dusky.

3
00:00:20.845 --> 00:00:22.706
"Coming up today?"

4
00:00:23.227 --> 00:00:24.508
asked Peter as usual.

5
00:00:24.528 --> 00:00:28.752
"Yes. The doctor is coming too," she replied.

6
00:00:30.252 --> 00:00:32.273
Peter glanced sideways at the doctor.

7
00:00:33.353 --> 00:00:39.515
Then, Grandfather came out, said good morning to the doctor, and hung a bag of food over Peter's

8
00:00:39.535 --> 00:00:45.856
shoulder. It was a little heavier than usual, and Peter grinned at the thought of what might be

9
00:00:45.896 --> 00:00:49.997
inside. They set off up the mountain.

10
00:00:51.018 --> 00:00:53.778
The goats surrounded Heidi until she waved them ahead.

11
00:00:53.798 --> 00:00:56.939
"Run along now," she said.

12
00:00:56.959 --> 00:00:59.820
"I want to walk with the doctor."

13
00:01:01.056 --> 00:01:06.300
Heidi happily chatted to the doctor about the goats and the flowers she wanted to show him.

14
00:01:08.862 --> 00:01:14.287
At a spot where they could look down on the distant valley and up to the snow sparkling

15
00:01:14.447 --> 00:01:16.849
on the mountain above, they sat down.

16
00:01:17.990 --> 00:01:21.393
The goat-bells tinkled pleasantly as the herd moved about.

17
00:01:22.694 --> 00:01:25.716
Heidi looked at the doctor to see if he was enjoying the scene.

18
00:01:27.478 --> 00:01:30.180
He could tell from her eyes what was on her mind.

19
00:01:31.272 --> 00:01:34.493
"Yes, Heidi, it's very beautiful," he said.

20
00:01:35.654 --> 00:01:42.577
He thought for a little about his daughter, who had died, and then asked, almost to himself, "Can

21
00:01:42.657 --> 00:01:45.698
a heart forget sorrow and be happy, even here?"

22
00:01:47.559 --> 00:01:50.140
"No one is sad here," Heidi answered.

23
00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:52.361
"Only in Frankfurt."

24
00:01:53.661 --> 00:01:55.662
A thoughtful expression crossed his face.

25
00:01:55.682 --> 00:02:00.484
"But what if you can't leave all the sadness behind in Frankfurt?"

26
00:02:01.012 --> 00:02:01.413
he said.

27
00:02:01.433 --> 00:02:08.759
"When there is nothing you can do," Heidi said confidently, "tell God."

28
00:02:08.779 --> 00:02:12.362
"Those are good words," said the doctor.

29
00:02:12.382 --> 00:02:19.988
"Can you understand that, even up here, sorrow can cast a shadow so that you can't really see

30
00:02:20.048 --> 00:02:20.649
all the beauty?"

31
00:02:22.330 --> 00:02:28.455
Heidi thought about his words, and they reminded her that Grannie would never see the sunlight or the

32
00:02:28.495 --> 00:02:33.914
mountains. Then, she said, "I can tell you one of Grannie's prayers.

33
00:02:35.234 --> 00:02:37.775
She says they always bring light to her heart."

34
00:02:39.376 --> 00:02:44.999
The doctor nodded, so Heidi clasped her hands together and recited Grannie's favorite prayer.

35
00:02:46.139 --> 00:02:50.961
She knew it well because Grannie always asked her to read it three times over.

36
00:02:52.042 --> 00:03:02.251
She ended with the last verse: To God confide your cares, On Him your burden cast, He hears

37
00:03:02.291 --> 00:03:06.595
your every prayer, And sends relief at last.

38
00:03:08.396 --> 00:03:10.758
The doctor listened with his eyes closed.

39
00:03:11.959 --> 00:03:17.043
It was the same verse that his mother often sang to him as a boy, and it cheered

40
00:03:17.103 --> 00:03:18.084
his heart greatly.

41
00:03:19.165 --> 00:03:22.788
He patted Heidi's hand and said, "Thank you, Heidi.

42
00:03:23.208 --> 00:03:24.329
We'll come up here again."

43
00:03:25.970 --> 00:03:27.992
All of this was not to Peter's liking.

44
00:03:29.036 --> 00:03:34.901
This was the first day in weeks that Heidi had come up the mountain, and now, she was

45
00:03:34.961 --> 00:03:36.842
sitting with the doctor the whole time.

46
00:03:37.943 --> 00:03:39.905
He kicked at the grass and scowled.

47
00:03:41.026 --> 00:03:47.331
At midday, when the sun was overhead, he ran up to them and shouted loudly, "Dinner time!"

48
00:03:49.052 --> 00:03:52.635
The doctor laughed, and they opened up the bag with the food.

49
00:03:53.776 --> 00:04:00.989
Heidi and the doctor shared most of their lunch with Peter, including a large, hearty sausage that Grandfather

50
00:04:01.049 --> 00:04:01.709
had included.

51
00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:08.992
For the rest of the month, the doctor often went for long walks with Grandfather in the clear

52
00:04:09.173 --> 00:04:13.755
air. He enjoyed just as much his trips up the mountain with Heidi.

53
00:04:14.815 --> 00:04:17.256
On his last day, he thanked them both.

54
00:04:18.917 --> 00:04:22.258
Heidi waved as he headed down to Dorfli one last time.

55
00:04:23.439 --> 00:04:29.449
The doctor turned for a final look and thought, "This is certainly a wonderful place for healing.

56
00:04:30.572 --> 00:04:32.475
Life seems really worth living again."
